From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:54:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Set the SD pin drive strength
 per pin

All six SD pins (PF0-PF5) are driven at 30 mA, which is too strong for
CMD and the data lines: SD reads at 3.3 V and 50 MHz fail now and then
with a data CRC and end-bit error.

Give the clock line PF2 a group of its own at 30 mA and set CMD and the
four data lines (PF0, PF1, PF3-PF5) to 10 mA, all with pull-ups.

Not covered: the card detect pin PF6 and a 1.8 V pad state.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the SD pins carry the new
drive strengths, and reading 256 MiB from the card gives no error.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index b9e7035b71dd..e28314652e67 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -311,15 +311,22 @@ pio: pinctrl@2000000 {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <3>;
 
-			mmc0_pins: mmc0-pins {
-				pins = "PF0", "PF1", "PF2",
-				       "PF3", "PF4", "PF5";
+			mmc0_clk_pin: mmc0-clk-pins {
+				pins = "PF2";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
 				function = "mmc0";
 				drive-strength = <30>;
 				bias-pull-up;
 			};
 
+			mmc0_pins: mmc0-pins {
+				pins = "PF0", "PF1", "PF3", "PF4", "PF5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc0";
+				drive-strength = <10>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+			};
+
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
@@ -431,7 +438,7 @@ mmc0: mmc@4020000 {
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_MMC0>;
 			reset-names = "ahb";
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
-			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc0_pins>;
+			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc0_pins>, <&mmc0_clk_pin>;
 			max-frequency = <200000000>;
 			cap-sd-highspeed;
 			status = "disabled";
